  "finalReply": "Done. `/app/convert_masks.py` is complete and verified end-to-end on the demo data.\n\n## What the script does\n- **MobileSAM (distilled SAM, `vit_t`) on CPU**: loads weights via `sam_model_registry[\"vit_t\"]`, encodes the RGB image once, then refines **every** mask in the CSV (rectangles and polylines alike) with a box prompt derived from its `xmin/ymin/xmax/ymax` columns — best of 3 masks by predicted score, using raw logits (`return_logits=True`). MobileSAM source is only imported, never modified; only allowed packages are imported.\n- **One contiguous mask per cell**: keeps the largest connected component of each SAM prediction; empty/degenerate boxes fall back to an inscribed ellipse/disk.\n- **No overlap**: per-pixel argmax over MobileSAM logits (restricted to a slightly dilated box per cell), then an iterative `cv2.fillPoly`-based deconfliction loop that re-rasterizes all output polygons and re-extracts exact contours until zero pixels are contested (priority: SAM score → smaller area → input order). Fully emptied cells get a small carved-out disk so every row keeps exactly one mask.\n- **All polylines, never rectangular**: exact (unsimplified) contours; any near-box mask is replaced by an inscribed ellipse. Bounding columns are recomputed from the new rings, which are saved closed (last point = first, matching input convention).\n- **CSV fidelity**: same columns/row order; only the six geometry columns change; leading index header preserved; `output_path` accepts a directory (saves `<basename(csv_path)>` there) or a direct `.csv` file; args work as `--flags` or positionals.\n\n## Verification performed\n- Full run on `/app/demo_rgb.png` + `/app/demo_metadata.csv` (48 masks, CPU, ~12 s incl. model load).\n- Independent checker: 0 rectangular, 0 bbox mismatches, 0 multi-component, **0 overlaps under both cv2 and PIL rasterization**, all rings closed and in-bounds (max bbox fill 0.87, 28–114 vertices each).\n- Edge case: zero-area box row → valid 4×4 octagon mask, still overlap-free; `--flag=value` form and file-style `output_path` both work.",
